":1.0479704141081851,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.20525012358688763,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.05288728378339612,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":26.4,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5821434670790994,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":3.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.01522882454210601,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":21.7,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.017757910413454564,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":39.3,"_gate_pool_share":0.06749345625451175,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":67.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02245173823311593,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":36.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05495464402903494,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0007169671017502569,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.82241994,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"HighPeak Energy, Inc. operates as an independent crude oil and natural gas exploration and production company. It engages in the exploration, development, and production of crude oil, natural gas, and natural gas liquids reserves in the Permian Basin in West Texas and Eastern New Mexico. The company was formerly known as HPK Energy, LP and changed its name to HighPeak Energy, Inc. in August 2020. The company was founded in 2019 and is headquartered in Fort Worth, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven W. Tholen | Chief Financial Officer | Age 74 | Compensation: $883,400 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 50 people. Revenue per employee of $17.3M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers, with revenue growing 41%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $10.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["HighPeak Energy, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $931M market cap on $863M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -7.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $512M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 26.98\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 82% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -7.2pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (41.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 123% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 91% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (HPK) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_HPK_That_Institutions_Follow_112126052401_1795299841.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795299841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273